      "message": "For all the java profiles, the `start` is a lie.\n\nIt is always (no exception) called right after the constructor and only after the constructor.\n\nWe do not support `start` -\u003e `cleanup` -\u003e `start` and this is never done in the code, we always do `constructor` -\u003e `start` -\u003e `cleanup`.\n\nThere is ongoing plan to simply inline start in the constructor, to allow more variable to be final.\n\n\nBut you are right about `mStateMachinesThread` being assigned to null, this is not great. I moved the variable to final to reflet that it can never be changed once set.",
