      "message": "Agreed that there is a defacto continuation from constructor to `start()` and inlining them is indeed good idea to stay truthful to how it works. \n\nHowever, before the inlining work happens, this code still have `start()` and `cleanup()` and we should stick to it and only modifying it during the inlining effort. \n\nHence, may I suggest keeping logic like\n\n```\nif (mStateMachinesThread !\u003d null) {\n  mStateMachinesThread.start();\n  mStateMachinesLooper \u003d mStateMachinesThread.getLooper();\n}\n```\n\nhere to match the logic in `cleanup()`?\n\nYou can move them to constructor while inlining constructor and `start()` later",
